{
  "$schema": "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",

  // Intentionally no regexManagers.
  //
  // `runs.using` in a JavaScript action manifest is not a free version pin: the
  // GitHub Actions runner only accepts a fixed set of runtimes (`node20`,
  // `node24` as of 2026-11). Rewriting it from the repo's `.mise.toml` node pin
  // makes Renovate produce manifests that the runner refuses to load and that
  // actionlint rejects:
  //
  //   invalid runner name "node26" at runs.using ... valid runners are
  //   "composite", "docker", "node20", and "node24"
  //
  // That is exactly what broke the node 24 -> 26 PRs in action-folder-matrix,
  // action-semver-release and action-calver-release: the `.mise.toml` hunk was
  // correct, the `action.yml` `using:` hunk was invalid, so the lint job failed
  // and every consumer workflow would have failed to load the action.
  //
  // `.mise.toml` keeps moving through the `mise` manager. Bump `runs.using` by
  // hand only once GitHub publishes support for the new runtime.
}
